{"type":"compaction","id":"06e875fd","parentId":"1b9bf561","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:20:42.148Z","summary":"## Goal\n- Run the crypto news pipeline end-to-end for the user.\n- Diagnose why the article did not include a chart image.\n- Identify which agent/tool is responsible for chart generation after recent config updates.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- User asked for explanation/diagnosis only when discussing the chart issue: “do not attempt anything,” “do not add anything,” “without breaking or changing anything.”\n- User prefers direct answers about ownership/responsibility for chart generation.\n- Native Telegram exec approvals are not configured; approvals appear in Web UI or terminal UI only.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Started and completed research step with `researcher`.\n- [x] Saved research JSON to `/tmp/research.json`.\n- [x] Research topic identified: **CLARITY Act momentum lifts Bitcoin sentiment and crypto regulation hopes**.\n- [x] Triggered writer step after approval issues were resolved.\n- [x] Detected writer output quality issue: `/tmp/crypto-article.md` was polluted with terminal spinner/ANSI noise, causing misleading word counts.\n- [x] Manually rewrote/cleaned `/tmp/crypto-article.md` into a usable final article ending with `[Word Count: 1094]`.\n- [x] Generated feature image at `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg`.\n- [x] Created/uploaded DOCX to Google Drive and returned link: `https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LDO6zo47zLWJwa5gXz_Hgvfq0Wpl4dux/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=109667066179998081561&rtpof=true&sd=true`\n- [x] Diagnosed the missing chart as a **verification/insertion gap**, not an approval problem.\n- [x] Confirmed available chart tooling via `~/.openclaw/skills/chart-generator/SKILL.md`.\n- [x] Read updated local config files:\n  - `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md`\n  - `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/AGENTS.md`\n  - `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/TOOLS.md`\n- [x] Concluded updated config now defines a specialized **`chart-generator` agent** at **Step 2.5**.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Evaluating the updated chart-generation flow and whether chart embedding into the article/doc is explicitly handled.\n\n### Blocked\n- No immediate execution block for diagnosis-only discussion.\n- If more commands are needed later, Telegram native approvals are still not configured:\n  - `Exec approval is required, but native chat exec approvals are not configured on Telegram.`\n- Earlier writer command also hit:\n  - `Exec denied (gateway id=838243b4-a407-475a-903c-24821f5b58b9, approval-timeout (allowlist-miss))`\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Chart issue was not caused by approvals**: The assistant concluded approvals were fine; the failure was that chart generation/insertion was not executed and/or verified before export/publish.\n- **Writer should not own chart creation**: Writer may place `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]`, but actual chart work should be handled by a dedicated chart path.\n- **Use chart-specific tool/agent for charts**: Initially confirmed `chart-generator` skill exists; after config update, concluded there is now a dedicated `chart-generator` agent in the pipeline.\n- **Do not modify system while diagnosing**: User explicitly wanted explanation only, so no further changes/actions were taken during diagnosis.\n- **Clean article file manually**: Because `/tmp/crypto-article.md` had ANSI/spinner noise, the assistant overwrote it with a clean final version rather than trusting raw `wc` output.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Verify the updated `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md` Step 2.5 details for `chart-generator` end-to-end.\n2. Confirm whether `/tmp/chart.png` is explicitly inserted into markdown/doc before `pandoc`.\n3. If not explicit, identify the exact missing handoff: chart generation succeeded but embedding missing, or embedding step absent entirely.\n4. Keep diagnosis-only unless the user asks to fix the pipeline.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Research file: `/tmp/research.json`\n- Final cleaned article file: `/tmp/crypto-article.md`\n- Feature image file: `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg`\n- The cleaned article still contains `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` markers; this is central to the bug diagnosis.\n- Relevant chart skill file:\n  - `~/.openclaw/skills/chart-generator/SKILL.md`\n  - It says to run:\n    - `python3 {baseDir}/scripts/generate_chart.py --coin {CHART_COIN} --days {CHART_DAYS} --output {CHART_OUTPUT}`\n- Updated orchestrator finding from `SOUL.md`:\n  - Specialized **`chart-generator` agent**\n  - Runs at **Step 2.5**\n  - Uses:\n    - `CHART_COIN`\n    - `CHART_DAYS: 30`\n    - `CHART_OUTPUT: /tmp/chart.png`\n  - Proceed on `CHART_DONE:`\n  - Skip on `CHART_ERROR:`\n- Assistant’s latest conclusion: generation responsibility now looks correct, but **chart embedding/verification still may be missing**, because publish flow explicitly embeds only the feature image:\n  - `printf '![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)\\n\\n' | cat - /tmp/crypto-article.md > /tmp/crypto-with-image.md`\n  - `pandoc /tmp/crypto-with-image.md -o /tmp/crypto-article.docx --standalone`\n- Prior pipeline agents used/identified:\n  - `researcher`\n  - `writer`\n  - `creator`\n  - `publisher`\n  - `wp-publisher`\n  - orchestrator/Nexus\n- The user is currently focused on **who should do chart work** and whether the updated setup correctly handles it.\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\n[The user asked to start the crypto pipeline fresh, after clearing agent sessions.]\n\n## Early Progress\n- [Assistant acknowledged a fresh restart and said it would clear sessions as it went.]\n- [Assistant began with Step 1 — Research.]\n- [It deleted the researcher agent session file: `~/.openclaw/agents/researcher/sessions/sessions.json`.]\n- [It launched the `researcher` agent from `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator` with instructions to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, identify the single biggest news event, and return aggregated Single-Topic JSON.]\n- [The visible tool output in the prefix mostly shows OpenClaw startup and “Waiting for agent reply…”, with no completed research result yet in the retained prefix.]\n\n## Context for Suffix\n- [This turn is a fresh pipeline run, so prior agent state should be treated as cleared/reset.]\n- [The pipeline had only started the researcher stage in the prefix; later retained work likely continues from or handles the researcher output.]\n- [No final research JSON or downstream agent steps are present in the kept prefix, so any such results would appear in the suffix.]\n\n<read-files>\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/AGENTS.md\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/TOOLS.md\n~/.openclaw/skills/chart-generator/SKILL.md\n</read-files>\n\n<modified-files>\n/tmp/crypto-article.md\n/tmp/research.json\n</modified-files>","firstKeptEntryId":"464725fc","tokensBefore":135612,"details":{"readFiles":["/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/AGENTS.md","/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md","/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/TOOLS.md","~/.openclaw/skills/chart-generator/SKILL.md"],"modifiedFiles":["/tmp/crypto-article.md","/tmp/research.json"]},"fromHook":false}
